                </p>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center">

            <!-- Left Content -->
            <div class="col-lg-7">

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    <strong>Chartered Accountancy (CA)</strong> is one of the most prestigious professional qualifications in India, governed and awarded by the
                    <strong>Institute of Chartered Accountants of India (ICAI)</strong>.
                    ICAI is one of the largest accounting bodies in the world, and the CA designation it grants is recognised across India as well as in several international jurisdictions.
                </p>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    A <strong>Chartered Accountant</strong> is a qualified finance and accounting professional authorised to audit company accounts, provide financial advisory services, manage taxation, and ensure regulatory compliance.
                    Businesses of every size, from startups to Fortune 500 companies, rely on Chartered Accountants for critical financial decisions.
                </p>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    The CA course is structured into three progressive levels:
                    <strong>CA Foundation</strong>,
                    <strong>CA Intermediate</strong>, and
                    <strong>CA Final</strong>.
                    Students also complete a mandatory
                    <strong>2.5-year Articleship</strong> (practical training under an Experienced Chartered Accountant, updated as per the new ICAI syllabus) alongside their Intermediate and Final studies.
                    This unique combination of rigorous theoretical examinations and practical industry training makes the CA qualification highly valuable in today's job market.
                </p>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    As per the updated ICAI syllabus,
                    <strong>CA Foundation</strong> and
                    <strong>CA Intermediate</strong> examinations are now conducted
                    <strong>three times every year</strong> in
                    <strong>January, May, and September</strong>, giving students more frequent and structured opportunities to progress.
                    <strong>CA Final</strong> continues to be conducted
                    <strong>twice a year</strong> in
                    <strong>May</strong> and
                    <strong>November</strong>.
                </p>

                <p class="text-muted">
                    Each level develops a different set of competencies.
                    <strong>Foundation</strong> builds strong fundamentals,
                    <strong>Intermediate</strong> strengthens technical expertise in law, accounts, costing, and taxation,
                    while <strong>Final</strong> focuses on advanced financial reporting, strategic management, and direct & indirect taxation.
                </p>

            </div>

            <!-- Right Side Cards -->
            <div class="col-lg-5 mt-5 mt-lg-0">

